Build bookworm-uefi sdcard image for raspberrypi4b:

cd ~/Downloads
wget https://mirror.us.mirhosting.net/debian-cd/12.11.0/arm64/iso-cd/debian-12.11.0-arm64-netinst.iso

cd ~/build-raspberrypi4b/bookworm-uefi

Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo ./mksdcardimg.sh
sudo mkfs.vfat /dev/sda1
sudo fdisk -l /dev/sda
sudo mount -t vfat /dev/sda1 /mnt
sudo 7z x ~/Downloads/debian-12.11.0-arm64-netinst.iso -o/mnt
sudo 7z x ~/Downloads/RPi4_UEFI_Firmware.zip -o/mnt
sync; sudo umount /mnt;
Eject usb3 stick from PC.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Install bookworm to usb3 stick.
NOTE: To minimize EMI interference, put usb3 stick to rpi4b top USB3 socket,
      Put keyboard mouse to rpi4b bottom USB2 socket with USB2 extention cable.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Plugin usb3 stick and ethernet cable to rpi4b. Power on rpi4b.
Esc -> Device Manager -> Rpi -> Advanced -> 3GB ( disable ) -> F10 -> Boot Manager -> first UEFI or SDCARD.
Select install
loading missing firmware? No
Select debian desktop and gnome in addition to ssh and standard system utilities.
User name: linaro

Disable power saving, auto suspend and screen saver.
su -
usermod -aG adm,sudo,video linaro
sync
shutdown -h now

Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo cp ./packages/brcmfmac43455-sdio.txt /media/$USER/*/lib/firmware/brcm/
sudo cp ./packages/BCM4345C0.hcd /media/$USER/*/lib/firmware/brcm/
sudo mkdir -p /media/$USER/*/lib/firmware/rtl_bt
sudo cp ./packages/rtl* /media/$USER/*/lib/firmware/rtl_bt
ls -la /media/$USER/*/lib/firmware/rtl_bt
sync
Umount, Eject usb3 stick from PC. 

Plugin usb3 stick to rpi4b, Unplug ethernet cable from rpi4b. Power on rpi4b.
Setup wifi.
sudo apt install openssh-server net-tools pulseaudio-utils
sudo ifconfig
uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo apt update; sudo apt upgrade;
sync
free
Check if Debian is running UEFI mode:
ls /sys/firmware/efi
Check display mode: ( wayland or x11 )
echo $XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Check audio driver: ( pulseaudio or pipewire )
pactl info

sudo apt install build-essential speedtest-cli python3-pip python3-setuptools ffmpeg mpv glmark2-es2-wayland pandoc vlc vlc-plugin-video-output pavucontrol rfkill firmware-realtek

speedtest-cli --secure

glmark2-es2-wayland

aplay -l

sudo rfkill list

mainline kernel 6.1.0-41-arm64 doesn't support rpi4b sound, GPU and bluetooth.
sudo shutdown -h now

---------------------------------------------------------------
Install vendor kernel 6.18.y
---------------------------------------------------------------

See ../kernel/README to compile vendor's kernel on PC. Then copy the resulting files to the Pi’s /boot and /lib/modules/.
Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo cp -r ../kernel/linux/tmp/lib/modules/* /media/$USER/*/lib/modules
sudo cp -r ../kernel/linux/tmp/boot/* /media/$USER/*/boot
sync
Umount, Eject usb3 stick from PC.

Boot rpi4b with old kernel.
ls -la /boot
df .
sudo e2label /dev/sda2 rootfs
sudo blkid /dev/sda2   ( look for LABEL and UUID )

sudo vi /etc/grub.d/40_custom_uuid ( add
#!/bin/sh
exec tail -n +3 $0

menuentry "Boot from UUID" {
    search --no-floppy --fs-uuid --set=root --hint='usb0,gpt2' --hint='mmcblk0,gpt2' --hint='mmcblk1,gpt2' 6c7dc7fc-848c-4a32-892d-de24e4dfad0d
    echo    'Loading Linux 6.18.0-rc5-v8+ ...'
    linux /boot/vmlinuz-6.18.0-rc5-v8+ root=LABEL=rootfs rootwait rw
    echo    'Loading initial ramdisk ...'
    initrd /boot/initrd.img-6.18.0-rc5-v8+
    devicetree /boot/dtb/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-4-b.dtb
}
)

Note: change the above UUID to real UUID like: b3adbe54-ab88-4da5-a9a6-08cf87a09d69

sudo chmod +x /etc/grub.d/40_custom_uuid

sudo vi /etc/default/grub ( change GRUB_DEFAULT=0 to GRUB_DEFAULT="Boot from UUID" )
sudo update-grub  ( generate grub.cfg )
sudo update-initramfs -c -k 6.18.0-rc5-v8+
sync
sudo reboot

uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo cat /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_cur_freq
Check if Debian is running UEFI mode:
ls /sys/firmware/efi

sudo apt install git zip speedtest-cli python3-pip python3-setuptools firefox-esr vsftpd

speedtest-cli --secure

glmark2-es2-wayland

aplay -l
pavucontrol  ( select hdmi as default )

firefox -> youtube.com -> search YmDNhi07_Ho

Do follows on PC, then ftp swan.mp4 to rpi4b.
(
git clone https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp.git
cd yt-dlp
make
cd ../
~/yt-dlp/yt-dlp -f 'bestvideo[ext=mp4][protocol=https]+bestaudio[ext=m4a][protocol=https]' 3qrKjywjo7Q -o swan.mp4 --postprocessor-args " -c:v libx264 -b:v 2M -c:a copy"
)

mpv swan.mp4
ffplay swan.mp4
cvlc --gl=wgl --glconv=any swan.mp4

Plugin ASUS USB-BT500 bluetooth usb dongle to rpi4b.
sudo rfkill list
hciconfig hci0
hcitool dev
hciconfig -a
